This extension adds The Last of Us Part II Remastered modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]ndarc tool and ND Mod Loader automatically installed.[/summary]

[b][size=3][color=#b6d7a8]This extension will automatically download and install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastofuspart2/mods/31]ndarc[/url]. You can use this tool to extract the vanilla .psarc game files.[/color] [color=#ea9999]YOU MUST DO THIS STEP FOR LOOSE DATA MODS TO WORK! [color=#b6d7a8]You will receive a Vortex notification where you can do the extraction.[/color][/color][/size]
[size=3][color=#ffff00]The extension will automatically download the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastofuspart2/mods/32]ndmodloader[/url], which allows for loading whole .psarc files. The extension will write all your .psarc mods to the modloader.ini and chunks.txt files based on the Load Order you set in Vortex![/color][/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]ND Mod Loader installs to the game folder, recognised by a "winmm.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Mod Loader mods with a ".psarc" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Build Folder mods with a "build" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Bin Folder mods with a "bin" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file install to the "build\pc\main" folder.[/*]
[*]Pak (actor97) mods with a ".pak" file install to the "build\pc\main" folder.[/*]
[*]Build Folder mods with a "build" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Save mods with a "USR-DATA" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Documents\The Last of Us Part II\<User ID>\savedata" folder.[/*]
[*]Config mods with a "screeninfo.cfg" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\SOFTWARE\Naughty Dog\The Last of Us Part II" folder.[/*]
[*]Ndarc Tool mods with a "ndarc.exe" file install to the "build\pc\main" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Whole .psarc files will be installed to the "mods" folder to be loaded by ndmodloader. You can set the Load Order for these mods in the Load Order tab. [color=#ffe599][b]The .psarc load order is written to the "modloader.ini"  and "chunks.txt" files automatically![/b] [/color]The files will also be reset if you Purge mods in Vortex.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for The Last of Us Part II Remastered mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

ND Mod Loader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "winmm.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

.psarc (Mod Loader):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".psarc" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Build Folder Pak Bin:

Recognised when the archive contains a "build" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

bin Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "bin" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file.

  Installs to: "build\pc\main"

========================================================================

Pak (actor97):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".pak" file.

  Installs to: "build\pc\main"

========================================================================

Build Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "build" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files, deployed to the game's save folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "USR-DATA".

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Documents\The Last of Us Part II\<User ID>\savedata"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod makes the archive install as a save.

========================================================================

Config File Mods:

Configuration tweaks, deployed to the game's config location.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "screeninfo.cfg".

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\SOFTWARE\Naughty Dog\The Last of Us Part II"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping a config file with one of these names inside an unrelated mod makes the whole archive install as a config mod.

========================================================================

ndarc Tool:

Recognised when the archive contains a "ndarc.exe" file.

  Installs to: "build\pc\main"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
